            "heading_path": "Contact Us",
            "text": "Heading: Contact Us\n\nContact Us",
            "token_count": 7,
            "source_spans": [
              {
                "start": 0,
                "end": 10,
                "kind": "paragraph"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "position": 2,
            "chunk_id": "e0a2d35c88eb09c11acd18e63ff5fc32f7f3c9f805588aa766ca51267ddd362b",
            "heading_path": "Bears and Food Storage",
            "text": "Heading: Bears and Food Storage\n\nBears and Food Storage\n\n\u00a9 Jeffrey Brooker\n\nYosemite National Park is home to hundreds of American black bears ; these bears have a voracious appetite. They also are incredibly curious and have an amazing sense of smell. This combination tempts them to seek our high-calorie food. Sometimes bears that routinely get our food become aggressive, and sometimes have to be killed as a result. By storing your food properly, you can prevent a bear's unnecessary death.\n\nPlease note that these food storage regulations have the force and effect of federal law: Failure to store your food properly may result in impoundment of your food or car and/or a fine of up to $5,000 and/or removal from your campsite or lodging facility.",
            "token_count": 155,
            "source_spans": [
              {
                "start": 12,
                "end": 34,
                "kind": "paragraph"
              },
              {
                "start": 36,
                "end": 53,
                "kind": "paragraph"
              },
              {
                "start": 55,
                "end": 474,
                "kind": "paragraph"
              },
              {
                "start": 476,
                "end": 732,
                "kind": "paragraph"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "position": 3,
            "chunk_id": "0cb9bf3c4652264fe6f87de61062843e3248883d36faa088fde2e212e1e11fe8",
            "heading_path": "Bears and Food Storage > What is Food?",
            "text": "Heading: Bears and Food Storage > What is Food?\n\nWhat is Food?\n\n\"Food\" includes any item with a scent, regardless of packaging. This may include items that you do not consider food, such as\n\ncanned goods\n\nbottles\n\ndrinks\n\nsoaps\n\ncosmetics\n\ntoiletries\n\ntrash\n\nice chests (even when empty, and even if certified as bear resistant)\n\nunwashed items used for preparing or eating meals.\n\nAll these items must be stored properly.",
            "token_count": 100,
            "source_spans": [
